      "relevance": "This is the introduction point of the xxh64 hashing context and its (un)serialization surface that allows attacker-controlled state fields (e.g., buffer length counters) to reach XXH64_update/XXH_INLINE_XXH64_update and drive an out-of-bounds memcpy length.")
