  "vulnerability_origin": "Likely introduced when xxHash support was added (commit 23590f7c…), by exposing XXH64_state_t to php_hash_unserialize without validating internal invariants (notably the internal 32-byte buffer length/counters). A crafted serialized context can set a length field > 32 causing size underflow/overflow and a huge memcpy read in XXH64_update.",
  "fix_hints": "History shows xxh64 uses generic php_hash_unserialize with a static pack spec (PHP_XXH64_SPEC) rather than a dedicated safe unserializer. A robust fix is to stop trusting serialized state fields and enforce bounds (especially the 32-byte internal buffer ‘memsize’ / similar) before any update call.",
  "fix_suggestions": [
    {
      "approach": "Implement custom serialize/unserialize for xxh32/xxh64 (replace php_hash_serialize/php_hash_unserialize) that validates all XXH*_state_t fields and rejects invalid states (e.g., memsize > 31, negative/overflowed totals).",
      "reasoning": "The vulnerable surface comes from generic unserialization of an internal C struct. Custom code can enforce invariants expected by xxHash before calling XXH*_update, preventing underflow/huge memcpy sizes.",
      "trade_offs": "More code to maintain; serialized format may become incompatible with previous versions unless you keep backward compatibility logic."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Defense-in-depth: add a state-sanity check in PHP_XXH64Update (and similar) before calling XXH64_update (e.g., if ctx->s.memsize > 31 then reset or error).",
      "reasoning": "Even if an invalid state slips through unserialize/copy, update becomes a hard barrier against corrupted invariants. Quick to implement.",
      "trade_offs": "Relies on knowledge of xxHash internals; may need updates if bundled xxHash struct layout changes."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Remove/disable serialization support for xxh32/xxh64 contexts entirely (like xxh3/xxh128 were intentionally not serialized) or only serialize minimal safe fields (seed/total length) and reinitialize buffers.",
      "reasoning": "Commit message already shows security-minded choice to avoid xxh3/xxh128 serialization due to secrets. Similar reasoning applies here: serializing raw internal state is brittle and unsafe.",
      "trade_offs": "Behavior change: existing serialized xxh32/xxh64 contexts would no longer round-trip; could break apps relying on it."
